  subgraph n052["Attention shape strategy: dense grid today, and planned flash attention"]
    direction TB
    subgraph n053[" "]
      direction LR
      subgraph n054["A · Dense grid, the strategy shown above"]
        direction TB
        n055["Pack the ragged flat list into a rectangle, so every  <br/>shape is fixed at compile time.  <br/>Needed because an offset computed from data does not  <br/>lower under compilation (torch-spyre#35;3508) — exactly  <br/>the arithmetic that flash relies on.  <br/>Eager tolerates it; compiled mode, our target, does not.<br/><br/>· build an additive mask [S, 1, L, L] marking padding  <br/>and cross-request slots  <br/>· build three index lists, then gather Q / K / V into  <br/>[S, H, L, D]  <br/>· one fused SDPA kernel per (S, L), then gather the  <br/>results back out<br/><br/>**Shape axes: T for the body, (S, L) for attention.  <br/>Two sets of buckets to warm.**<br/><br/>Costs: the mask grows with L², plus index lists and a  <br/>barrier per gather.  <br/>Works today. This is the current implementation."]
      end
      subgraph n056["B · Flash-style attention, planned"]
        direction TB
        n057["Never materialise the rectangle.  <br/>Each block of queries reads its request's offset from  <br/>the metadata at runtime, and works directly on the flat  <br/>list, carrying a running softmax maximum and sum.  <br/>That is the online-softmax structure the Spyre decoder  <br/>already uses over KV pages.<br/><br/>· no [S, 1, L, L] mask; request boundaries are the offsets  <br/>· no gather_pack / gather_unpack; the kernel reads the  <br/>flat list directly  <br/>· no per-layer index lists, so no per-gather barriers<br/><br/>**Shape axis: block count, bucketed like the decoder's  <br/>page loop. L disappears.**<br/><br/>Both upstream backends already work this way, neither  <br/>padding into a rectangle.  <br/>Flash attention consumes the flat list with  <br/>cu_seqlens_q = query_start_loc, and the CPU backend  <br/>passes query[:num_actual_tokens] to a C++ kernel."]
      end
    end
    subgraph n058[" "]
      direction LR
      subgraph n059["If flash attention lands, the design converges on upstream"]
        direction TB
        n060["· the second shape axis collapses; bucket T and a block count,  <br/>much closer to upstream's single axis  <br/>· the batch-shape tables box disappears, and with it the  <br/>per-layer rebuild problem and its barriers  <br/>· gather_pack / SDPA / gather_unpack collapse into one  <br/>blocked-attention kernel  <br/>· the mask's L² growth at long prompts disappears, today's  <br/>largest untested risk<br/><br/>Open question: whether a Spyre kernel can do the runtime  <br/>offset arithmetic this depends on. If it cannot, the block  <br/>count stays bucketed.  <br/>Everything else holds either way: padding seam, unpadded  <br/>metadata, warmup, compilation mode."]
      end
